
Suddenly I felt as if I had more to say.

------------- Rage against the dying of the disk -----------
Do not go slowly into that good server,
Old disks should spin and seek at close of file;
Rage, rage against the dying of the disk.

Though write cache is fast wise men will not waver,
Because forking data without trust is like cold bile.
Rage, rage against the dying of the disk.

Good men, disable write cache, crying how right
Their frail Sparc 5 might have danced with fibre array,
Rage, rage against the dying of the disk.

Wild men who caught and sang the Solaris in flight,
And learn, too late, they grieved Linux on its way,
Do not go gentle into that good night.

Grave Sparc, near death, will seek with blinding photon
Blind panic will blaze while Opterons sing a new day,
Oh William, Oh William where is your Joy?
Rage, rage against the dying of the disk.

And you, my Sparc, there with sad Alpha chip,
Curse, watch as x86 Solaris holds back the dawn,
Do not go gentle into that good night.
Rage, rage against the dying of the disk.


    With apologies to Dylan Thomas
    from Dennis dclarke@blastwave.org
    ( written somewhere in 1994 or so )

